              "stdout": "<class 'list'>\n[{'type': 'web_search_result', 'title': 'British schools in Bangkok: curriculum, fees and how to choose', 'url': 'https://www.ischooladvisor.com/articles/schooling-and-school-choice/guide-to-choosing-a-school/british-schools-in-bangkok-curriculum-fees-and-how-to-choose', 'content': \"Quick answer: Which British schools in Bangkok should you look at, and what do they cost? Bangkok Patana, Shrewsbury and Harrow follow the English curriculum through IGCSE to A Levels or the IB Diploma, and Dulwich College Bangkok opened in 2026…\\n\\n# British schools in Bangkok: curriculum, fees and how to choose\\n**Quick answer: Which British schools in Bangkok should you look at, and what do they cost?** Bangkok Patana, Shrewsbury and Harrow follow the English curriculum through IGCSE to A Levels or the IB Diploma, and Dulwich College Bangkok opened in 2026 with Nursery to Year 7.\\n\\n- FOBISIA, the association of British international schools in Asia, lists 29 member schools in Thailand, including Bangkok Patana, Harrow Bangkok and both Shrewsbury campuses.\\n\\n## What does a British school in Bangkok teach?\\nNot every English school in Bangkok ends with A Levels: Bangkok Patana teaches IGCSE and then the IB Diploma, and Dulwich College Bangkok says its students will choose between A Levels and the IB.\\n\\n## British schools in Bangkok to shortlist\\n### Bangkok Patana School\\n\\n### Harrow International School Bangkok\\nOther British schools in or near Bangkok on FOBISIA's list include Brighton College, Wellington College, King's College, Rugby School Thailand and the St Andrews schools.\\n\\n## How much do British schools in Bangkok cost in 2026-27?\\n\\n### Do British schools in Bangkok offer A Levels or the IB Diploma?\\nMost follow the English curriculum to IGCSE at 16 and then offer A Levels, as Shrewsbury and Harrow do, where sixth formers choose three or four subjects.\", 'page_age': '3 days ago'}, {'type': 'web_search_result',